WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.117
- You know my next guest from "Black-ish,"

00:00:02.117 --> 00:00:04.807
"Grown-ish," and his very
funny comedy special,

00:00:04.807 --> 00:00:07.490
"Cole Hearted," which is
now streaming on Netflix.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.390
Let's get him on in here, Deon Cole,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.223
can you hear me?

00:00:10.223 --> 00:00:11.294
Yes.
- What's up, girl?

00:00:11.294 --> 00:00:13.218
- Hi, Deon, how ya doing?

00:00:13.218 --> 00:00:14.530
- I'm good, how you doing?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.363
- I'm good.

00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:17.500
I don't know if I saw your
arms last time on the show.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.995
I like your tats, your artwork.

00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:21.234
- Oh thanks, man.

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:23.844
Yeah, probably was
covered up with my jacket.

00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:26.560
- Yes, and your beard game is on point.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.630
I like it.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.626
- Yeah, man.

00:00:28.626 --> 00:00:32.017
This quarantine beard. (laughs)

00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:33.280
- The quarantine beard.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.832
That will be the fashion of 2020.

00:00:34.832 --> 00:00:36.948
(laughing)

00:00:36.948 --> 00:00:39.970
I hear you've really taken
advantage of quarantine

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.320
by adding DJ to your resume, explain?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.940
- Yeah, so I've been DJing.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.000
I always had equipment for a long time,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.180
but I just never used it.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.880
But now I started using my equipment

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.140
and it's been great, man.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.360
Every Sunday, man, 11 a.m.,

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.457
West Coast time.

00:00:56.457 --> 00:00:57.690
We get it in,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.080
straight disco,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.828
disco, disco, disco, man.

00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:02.700
- That's fun, I love it!

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.230
And it's like, what a cool...

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.254
I think there's a lot of
us that buy things in hopes

00:01:07.254 --> 00:01:10.140
of things we wanna do
but we never get to do,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.260
so that's really cool that you
actually got in the cabinet,

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.450
got it out and did it. (laughs)

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.360
- Yeah, absolutely!

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.320
I mean when you go in...

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.780
I mean us bein' in this quarantine

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.230
and you cannot come outta
this not having a new skill,

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.470
or accomplishing something.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.850
You should know Spanish,

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.124
you should know French.

00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:26.957
(laughs)

00:01:26.957 --> 00:01:29.180
You should know all kinda languages.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.488
- Or you're just lazy.

00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:31.731
- Just something, you gotta
come out of this with something.

00:01:31.731 --> 00:01:32.880
Yeah, yeah, right. (laughs)

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.280
- All right, well on Instagram
you've been posting videos,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.710
looking for a new assistant,

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.630
so what are your requirements?

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.078
We wanna help you.

00:01:40.078 --> 00:01:41.780
- My requirements are:

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.480
I need someone to remind
me to call my mother,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.310
I also need to be reminded

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.130
to stop taking pictures with people

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.500
who don't think I'm worthy enough

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.342
to be posted on their page.

00:01:51.342 --> 00:01:52.175
- Oh, Amen.

00:01:52.175 --> 00:01:54.980
- Also, need to be outta the clubs

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.680
once we start going back to the clubs,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.440
I don't need to shut the club down.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.310
I'm always helping them clean
up at the end of the night,

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:03.973
so I need to leave 40
minutes earlier, please.

00:02:03.973 --> 00:02:04.806
(laughs)

00:02:04.806 --> 00:02:06.273
And yeah, yeah,

00:02:06.273 --> 00:02:07.597
those are my requirements.

00:02:07.597 --> 00:02:08.550
- You want someone helping you be

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:09.760
the best version of yourself.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.330
- I gotta be the best version of me.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.350
Just, and my clothes are expensive,

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.773
I have to really still be a nice person.

00:02:16.645 --> 00:02:18.895
(laughing)

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:21.542
- I love that you need
someone to remind you.

00:02:21.542 --> 00:02:22.420
- It's these requirements!

00:02:23.564 --> 00:02:25.100
Yeah, I have to know this.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.430
If I'm at the grocery store,

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.460
who's job is it to put the divider down,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.800
mine, or the person behind me?

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.692
I need an assistant to help
me with these things y'all.

00:02:34.692 --> 00:02:36.609
- God, I love you.

00:02:36.609 --> 00:02:40.247
Well, I mean I know that
there is a lot going on now,

00:02:40.247 --> 00:02:42.380
I mean not only just the pandemic,

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.130
but now not even just now,

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.120
it's been happening for awhile;

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.950
Black Lives Matter and generations

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.350
of trying to help this
change actually happen.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.240
And people are starting
to have the conversation

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.730
about what's going on in America,

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.530
and I know a lot of
people already knew that,

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.990
but a lot of people haven't,

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.270
and are listening at this point

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.470
that maybe weren't listening before.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.774
You guys, y'all been
doing that on "Black-ish"

00:03:04.774 --> 00:03:06.330
for a while now, right?

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.236
Just that conversation.

00:03:07.236 --> 00:03:10.940
- Yeah, we on the show
"Black-ish" that we do man,

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.780
we've always pushed the envelope

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:14.870
when it comes to race and situations,

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:17.110
and we try to inform people

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.590
as much as possible about certain things.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.330
I think some people
think it was just funny,

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.460
but it's real situations.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.510
We had one episode where it was just

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.130
a little white girl on the
elevator by herself and we,

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:33.070
the whole episode was
why we didn't get on.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.360
You're not getting on that
elevator with her. (laughs)

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.340
It might sound cruel but we like,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.542
look, I don't wanna be the guy

00:03:40.542 --> 00:03:42.290
that something happened to her,

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.160
I'm the person?

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.320
But we think like that.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.030
We live in a world right
now where it's like

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:47.863
we walk around--

00:03:47.863 --> 00:03:50.350
- And the fact that that's
normalized is not good,

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.083
that's not good.

00:03:52.083 --> 00:03:52.916
- No listen, listen,

00:03:52.916 --> 00:03:56.130
we're in a world where we
walk around as a black man,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:56.963
and black women,

00:03:56.963 --> 00:03:59.640
we walk around fearful all day long.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.660
Imagine this,

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.340
walking around being,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.707
feeling fear but being feared.

00:04:05.707 --> 00:04:07.530
It's like it's weird.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.260
It's like I'm being feared,

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.970
but you have no idea,

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.127
I'm just as scared as you are (chuckles)

00:04:14.127 --> 00:04:16.140
and you don't even realize that.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.500
- You're scared of the assumptions,

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.440
you're scared of the stereotyping.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.850
- The assumptions you have, yeah, yeah.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:24.320
So we tackle a lot of
problems like that, man.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.870
We always have and we just
got renewed for season seven

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.490
so I know this new
season is gonna be insane

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.290
with everything that's going
on and everything, so yeah.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.690
- Well I think what's important is

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:39.430
because y'all have and because
there are other shows too

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:41.860
that address that,

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.960
and even though it comes in a comedic way,

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:48.490
there's a seriousness there and
I think because that exists,

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.677
maybe it empowered people to go,

00:04:50.677 --> 00:04:53.060
"You know what, it's funny, but it's not."

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:53.893
- Yeah, I mean,

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.290
yeah, and see our mentality
in America is so different,

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.956
I remember one time I was at the,

00:05:01.956 --> 00:05:05.040
I left the Emmy's and went to
this bar and I was outside,

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.620
and I used to smoke
cigarettes at the time.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:09.320
I was smoking a cigarette
and I had a tuxedo on

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:10.717
and I was reflecting like,

00:05:10.717 --> 00:05:13.827
"Wow, I am from the South Side of Chicago

00:05:13.827 --> 00:05:15.170
"and I'm at the Emmy's!"

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:18.500
And this white woman walked
up to me and was like,

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.720
doin' this in my face,

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.460
and it was her valet ticket.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.926
- Ahhh!

00:05:23.926 --> 00:05:24.759
- She was like, "Here!"

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:26.750
And I was like this, "What?"

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:27.630
And I just was like,

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.923
wow, that's crazy.

00:05:28.923 --> 00:05:29.756
- I'm sorry.

00:05:29.756 --> 00:05:30.589
- Then I thought about it,

00:05:30.589 --> 00:05:34.119
I shoulda took the
ticket and took her car.

00:05:34.119 --> 00:05:36.369
(laughing)

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.510
- You were handing it out.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.260
- I missed my blessing, Kelly.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.954
That was my blessing.

00:05:42.954 --> 00:05:45.656
The Lord tried to bless me with a Mercedes

00:05:45.656 --> 00:05:47.890
and I didn't take it, Kelly.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.410
- No, I'm sorry.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:53.170
It's not only a hard thing to experience,

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.410
I can only imagine.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.260
But having kids,

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.790
and I know your son,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.320
he's 17-years-old,

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.590
I mean what are you say?

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.070
I mean I try and educate my
children as much as I can

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.440
with the age appropriate
information obviously,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.257
but you try and it's like
some things you're like,

00:06:10.257 --> 00:06:11.361
"God, I can't believe I have

00:06:11.361 --> 00:06:12.717
"to have this conversation with my kid?"

00:06:12.717 --> 00:06:13.760
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:16.027
- I can't imagine you having
to tell your boy like,

00:06:16.027 --> 00:06:17.200
"Hey, this is how it is."

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.911
That's not what you wanna tell your kid.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:21.310
- Yeah, I tell my son all the time, man.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.520
And it's not a good conversation
but it has to be had.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.977
I just always tell him,

00:06:25.977 --> 00:06:28.157
"Man, police ever mess
with you or whatever,

00:06:28.157 --> 00:06:31.530
"Just do what they say," and that's it.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:32.380
I mean you're right,

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:35.370
you have the right to say
and do whatever you want to,

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:39.040
but realistically we
want you to come home.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.180
Just comply,

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:42.140
do what you gotta do and come home.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.468
Don't say nothin'--
- That's sad.

00:06:44.468 --> 00:06:46.160
- Say the least that you
hafta say and that's it.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.180
And they might be doin' wrong to him.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.200
I still tell him,

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.970
just do what he has to do or
whatever in order to come home.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.580
Because there's a lot of
heroes that aren't here.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.450
And so I mean I want him to stand up

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.500
for how he feels or whatever,

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.210
but when he's by his self, at night,

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.260
and it's four police officers,

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.690
I need for you to come home.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:11.440
And then you come get me
and then we go deal with it.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.890
So I hafta let him know to
just do what he got to do

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:15.810
in order to get back to me, basically--

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:18.300
- I'm sorry you even have
to have that conversation.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.206
- Yeah, but it's like I said,

00:07:19.206 --> 00:07:23.650
it's a conversation that's been
going on for all our lives.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:27.040
My uncles and my grandfather taught me

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:31.323
and their uncles and their
grandfathers taught them,

00:07:31.323 --> 00:07:33.320
so it's just this mentality

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.070
that goes down and goes down or whatever.

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.030
But I tell ya this much,

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:40.510
white people are nice
as hell lately boy, woo!

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:41.670
They've been nice as hell.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:45.190
I was at the grocery store and
I had two customer services.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.300
I was like, this is... (laughs)

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.800
I was like this is all
right, boy I like this.

